{"questions":[{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607877","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607877","q":"<p><strong>Write the negation of the statement.</strong></p>\n<p>‘∃ n ∈ N such that n + 8 &gt; 11’</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>To negate the existential quantifier (∃), we use the logical rule:</p>\n<p>∼ (∃ n ∈ N, P (n)) ≡ ∀ n ∈ N, ∼ P(n)</p>\n<p>Here, P(n) is the statement n + 8 &gt; 11, so its negation is:</p>\n<p>n + 8 ≤ 11</p>\n<p>∀ n ∈ N, n + 8 ≤ 11</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860784b","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860784b","q":"<p><strong>Write the following compound statement symbolically.</strong></p>\n<p>Nagpur is in Maharashtra and Chennai is in Tamil Nadu. </p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let p: Nagpur is in Maharashtra.</p>\n<p>Let q: Chennai is in Tamil Nadu.</p>\n<p>Then the symbolic form of the given statement is p ∧ q.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860786f","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860786f","q":"<p>If A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} then which of the following is not true?</p>","options":["<p>∃ x ∈ A such that x + 3 = 8</p>","<p>∃ x ∈ A such that x + 2 &lt; 9</p>","<p>∀ x ∈ A, x + 6 ≥ 9</p>","<p>∃ x ∈ A such that x + 6 &lt; 10</p>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p><strong>∀ x ∈ A, x + 6 ≥ 9</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>Given set: A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}</p>\n<p><strong>1.</strong> ∃ x ∈ A such that x + 3 = 8</p>\n<p>This means there exists at least one x in A for which:</p>\n<p>x + 3 = 8</p>\n<p>x = 8 − 3</p>\n<p>x = 5</p>\n<p>Since 5 ∈ A, this statement is true.</p>\n<p><strong>2.</strong> ∃ x ∈ A such that x + 2 &lt; 9</p>\n<p>This means there exists at least one x in A for which:</p>\n<p>x + 2 &lt; 9</p>\n<p>Since for all values of x in A,</p>\n<p>1 + 2 = 3,</p>\n<p>2 + 2 = 4,</p>\n<p>3 + 2 = 5,</p>\n<p>4 + 2 = 6,</p>\n<p>5 + 2 = 7</p>\n<p>and all these values are less than 9, this statement is true.</p>\n<p><strong>3.</strong> ∀ x ∈ A, x + 6 ≥ 9</p>\n<p>This means for all x in A,</p>\n<p>x + 6 ≥ 9</p>\n<p>Checking each value of x:</p>\n<p> 1 + 6 = 7 (False, since 7 `≱ ` 9)</p>\n<p>Since one counterexample (x = 1) disproves the statement, this statement is false.</p>\n<p><strong>4.</strong> ∃ x ∈ A such that x + 6 &lt; 10</p>\n<p>This means there exists at least one x in A for which:</p>\n<p>x + 6 &lt; 10</p>\n<p>Checking each value of x:</p>\n<p>1 + 6 = 7,</p>\n<p>2 + 6 = 8,</p>\n<p>3 + 6 = 9,</p>\n<p>4 + 6 = 10,</p>\n<p>5 + 6 = 11</p>\n<p>Here, x = 1 satisfies 1 + 6 = 7 &lt; 10</p>\n<p>Since at least one x satisfies the condition, this statement is true.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860787b","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860787b","q":"<p>Using truth table, prove that the statement patterns p ↔ q and (p ∧ q) ∨ (~ p ∧ ~ q) are logically equivalent.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>p ↔ q ≡ (p ∧ q) ∨ (~ p ∧ ~ q)</p>\n<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>I</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>II</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>III</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>IV</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>V</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>VI</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>VII</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>VIII</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>p</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>~p<br/></strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>~q<br/></strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>p ↔ q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>p ∧ q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>~ p ∧ ~ q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>(p ∧ q) ∨ (~ p ∧ ~ q)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Columns V and VIII are identical.</p>\n<p>∴ p ↔ q ≡ (p ∧ q) ∨ (~ p ∧ ~ q)</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607843","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607843","q":"<p>The dual of statement t ∨ (p ∨ q) is ______.</p>","options":["<p>c ∧ (p ∨ q)</p>","<p>c ∧ (p ∧ q)</p>","<p>t ∧ (p ∧ q)</p>","<p>t ∧ (p ∨ q)</p>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>The dual of statement t ∨ (p ∨ q) is <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>c ∧ (p ∧ q)</strong></span>.</p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>Given statement is t ∨ (p ∨ q)</p>\n<p>Dual is c ∧ (p ∧ q)    ...(Basic concept)</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860784f","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860784f","q":"<p><strong>Construct the truth table for the statement pattern:</strong></p>\n<p>[(p → q) ∧ q] → p</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>p</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>(p → q)</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>[(p → q) ∧ q]</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>[(p → q) ∧ q]→ p</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">F</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607817","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607817","q":"<p>If p ∧ q is F, p → q is F then the truth values of p and q are ________.</p>","options":["<p>T, T</p>","<p>T, F </p>","<p>F, T</p>","<p>F, F</p>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>If p ∧ q is F, p → q is F then the truth values of p and q are <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>T, F</strong></span>.</p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>Consider the following truth table:</p>\n<table width=\"320\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>p</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>q</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>p ∧ q</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>p → q</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>If (p ∧ q) is F and (p → q) is F, the their truth value must be T and F respectively.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607823","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607823","q":"<p><strong>Write converse, inverse and contrapositive of the following statement.</strong></p>\n<p>If x &lt; y then x<sup>2</sup> &lt; y<sup>2</sup> (x, y ∈ R)</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let p: x &lt; y,<br/>      q: x<sup>2</sup> &lt; y<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p>Then the symbolic form of the given statement is p → q.</p>\n<p>Its converse is q → p.</p>\n<p>If x<sup>2</sup> &lt; y<sup>2</sup>, then x &lt; y.</p>\n<p>Its inverse is ∼p → ∼q.</p>\n<p>If x `≥` y, then x<sup>2</sup> `≥` y<sup>2</sup>.</p>\n<p>OR</p>\n<p>If x `≮` y, then x<sup>2</sup> `≮` y<sup>2</sup>.</p>\n<p>Its contrapositive is ∼q → ∼p.</p>\n<p>If x<sup>2</sup> `≥` y<sup>2</sup>, then x `≥` y.<br/>OR<strong><br/></strong>If x<sup>2</sup> `≮` y<sup>2</sup>, then x `≮` y.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077eb","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077eb","q":"<p>The negation of p ^ (q → r) is ______.</p>","options":["<p>∼ p ∧ (∼q →∼r)</p>","<p>p ∨ (∼q ∨∼r)</p>","<p>∼ p ∧ (∼q →r)</p>","<p>p → (q ∧∼r)</p>"],"answer":3,"solution":"<p>The negation of p ^ (q → r) is <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>p → (q ∧∼r)</strong></span>.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077f7","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077f7","q":"<p><strong>Using truth table verify that:</strong></p>\n<p>(p ∧ q)∨ ∼ q ≡ p∨ ∼ q</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">p</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">q</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">∼ q</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">p ∧ q</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(p ∧ q) ∨ ∼ q</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">p ∨ ∼ q</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>∴ (p ∧ q)∨ ∼ q ≡ p∨ ∼ q</p>\n<p>Hence proved.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077cd","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077cd","q":"<p>Write the truth values of the following statements:<br/>(1) 2 is a rational number and`sqrt2` is an irrational number. . <br/>(2) 2 + 3 = 5 or `sqrt 2 +sqrt3 = sqrt5`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>(1) Let p : 2  is rational number, q : `sqrt2`  is an irrational number. . So given compound statement is p ^ q. Truth value of of p is T and that q is T. Hence, truth value p ^ q = T ^ T =T.<br/>(2)  Let p = 2 + 3 = 5 which is T.<br/>q = `sqrt2 +sqrt3 =sqrt5`  which is F<br/>∴ Truth value of given statment is T ∨ F = T.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077a2","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077a2","q":"<p>Write the negations of the following statements :</p>\n<p>1) All students of this college live in the hostel</p>\n<p>2) 6 is an even number or 36 is a perfect square.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>1) p: All students of this college live in the hostel.</p>\n<p>Negation :</p>\n<p>~ p: Some students of this college do not live in the hostel.</p>\n<p>2) </p>\n<p>p: 6 is an even number.<br/>q: 36 is a perfect square.</p>\n<p>Symbolic form : p v q</p>\n<p>∴ ~(p v q) ≡ ~p ∧ ~q</p>\n<p>Negation :</p>\n<p>6 is not an even number and 36 is not a perfect square.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d14860777e","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d14860777e","q":"<p>Write the following statement in symbolic form and find its truth value:<br/>∀ n ∈ N, n<sup>2</sup> + n is an even number and n<sup>2</sup> - n is an odd number.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let p ≡ ∀ n ∈ N, n<sup>2</sup> + n is an even number</p>\n<p>Let q ≡ ∀ n ∈ N, n<sup>2</sup> - n is an odd number</p>\n<p>The symbolic form of given statement is<br/>(p ∧ q)</p>\n<p>Truth value of given statement is</p>\n<p>p ≡ ∀ n ∈ N, n<sup>2</sup> + n is an even number (T)</p>\n<p>q ≡ ∀ n ∈ N, n<sup>2</sup> - n is an odd number (F)</p>\n<p>(∵ from n = 1, n<sup>2</sup> - n = 0, which is not an odd number)</p>\n<p>∴ (p ∧ q) ≡ T ∧ F ≡ F</p>\n<p>∴ the given statement is false</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607887","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607887","q":"<p><strong>Find the symbolic form of the given switching circuit. Construct its switching table and interpret your result.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941b000e3720f1c028af50a.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941b000e3720f1c028af50a.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941b000e3720f1c028af50a.png?alt=media\"/></strong></p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let p, q denote the statements that the switches S<sub>1</sub>, S<sub>2</sub> are closed respectively.</p>\n<p>Let ~p, ~q denote the statements that switches `\"S\"_1^\"'\"` and `\"S\"_2^\"'\"` are closed respectively.</p>\n<p>The symbolic form of the given switching circuit is (p ∨ q) ∧ (~p ∧ ~q) ≡ l</p>\n<p>The switching table for the given switching circuit is as follows: </p>\n<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>1</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>2</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>3</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>4</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>5</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>6</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>7</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>p</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>~p</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>~q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>p ∨ q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>~p ∧ ~q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>5 ∧ 6</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>In the last column of the switching table, each entry is zero, i.e. it is a contradiction.</p>\n<p>Hence, no current will flow in the circuit irrespective of the positions of the switches.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860785b","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860785b","q":"<p><strong>Find the symbolic form of the given switching circuit. Construct its switching table and interpret your result.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941aff5e3720f1c028af505.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941aff5e3720f1c028af505.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941aff5e3720f1c028af505.png?alt=media\"/></strong></p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let p, q denote the statements that the switches S<sub>1</sub>, S<sub>2</sub> are closed respectively.</p>\n<p>Let ~p, ~q denote the statements that switches `\"S\"_1^\"'\"` and `\"S\"_2^\"'\"` are closed respectively.</p>\n<p>The symbolic form of the given switching circuit is (p ∨ q) ∧ (~p ∧ ~q) ≡ l</p>\n<p>The switching table for the given switching circuit is as follows: </p>\n<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>1</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>2</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>3</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>4</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>5</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>6</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>7</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>p</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>~p</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>~q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>p ∨ q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>~p ∧ ~q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>5 ∧ 6</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>In the last column of the switching table, each entry is zero, i.e. it is a contradiction.</p>\n<p>Hence, no current will flow in the circuit irrespective of the positions of the switches.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077a8","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077a8","q":"<p>Using the truth table, prove the following logical equivalence :</p>\n<p>p ↔ q ≡ (p ∧ q) ∨ (~p ∧ ~q)</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 76.8116%; height: 76px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 12.5%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\">1</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 12.5%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\">2</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 12.5%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\">3</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">4</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 12.5%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\">5</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 12.5%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\">6</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">7</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 12.5%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\">8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">A</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">p</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">q</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">p ↔ q</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">p ∧ q</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">~p</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">~q</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">~p ∧ ~q</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">A V B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n<p>T</p>\n<p>F</p>\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n<p>F</p>\n<p>T</p>\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">\n<p><strong>T</strong></p>\n<p><strong>F</strong></p>\n<p><strong>F</strong></p>\n<p><strong>T</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">\n<p>T</p>\n<p>F</p>\n<p>F</p>\n<p>F</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n<p>F</p>\n<p>T</p>\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n<p>T</p>\n<p>F</p>\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">\n<p>F</p>\n<p>F</p>\n<p>F</p>\n<p>T</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.5%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">\n<p><strong>T</strong></p>\n<p><strong>F</strong></p>\n<p><strong>F</strong></p>\n<p><strong>T</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>By column number 3 and 8</p>\n<p>p ↔ q ≡ (p ∧ q) ∨ (~p ∧ ~q)</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077af","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077af","q":"<p>Write converse, inverse and contrapositive of the following conditional statement :</p>\n<p>If an angle is a right angle then its measure is 90°.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p><strong>Converse</strong>: If the measure of an angle is 90° then it is a right angle</p>\n<p><strong>Inverse</strong> : If an angle is not a right angle then its measure is not 90°.</p>\n<p><strong>Contrapositive:</strong> If the measure of an angle is not 90° then it is not a right angle.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d14860777f","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d14860777f","q":"<p>Using truth tables, examine whether the statement pattern (p ∧ q) ∨ (p ∧ r) is a tautology, contradiction or contingency.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>No of rows = 2<sup>n</sup>=2<sup>3</sup> =8<br/>No. of columns = m+ n=3+3= 6</p>\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 329px; height: 173px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27px; height: 18px;\">p</td>\n<td style=\"width: 24px; height: 18px;\">q</td>\n<td style=\"width: 30px; height: 18px;\">r</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50px; height: 18px;\">p ∧ q</td>\n<td style=\"width: 45px; height: 18px;\">p ∧ r</td>\n<td style=\"width: 134px; height: 18px;\">(p ∧ q) ∨ (p ∧ r)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 24px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 30px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 45px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 134px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 24px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 30px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 45px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 134px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 17px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27px; height: 17px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 24px; height: 17px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 30px; height: 17px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50px; height: 17px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 45px; height: 17px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 134px; height: 17px;\">T</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 24px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 30px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 45px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 134px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 24px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 30px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 45px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 134px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 24px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 30px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 45px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 134px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 24px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 30px; height: 18px;\">T</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 45px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 134px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 27px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 24px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 30px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 45px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n<td style=\"width: 134px; height: 18px;\">F</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>In the last column, the truth values of the statement is neither all T nor all F. Hence, it is neither a tautology nor a contradiction i.e. it is a contingency.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d148607785","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d148607785","q":"<p>Construct the switching circuit for the statement (p ∧ q) ∨ (~ p) ∨ (p ∧ ~ q).</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let</p>\n<p>p = Switch `S_1` is closed<br/>q = Switch `S_2` is closed</p>\n<p>`~p= switch\" \" S_1^' and ~q-=S_2^'`</p>\n<p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941afcbe3720f1c028af4ed.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afcbe3720f1c028af4ed.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afcbe3720f1c028af4ed.png?alt=media\"/></p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860783b","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860783b","q":"<p>Simplify the given circuit by writing its logical expression. Also, write your conclusion.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941afefe3720f1c028af502.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afefe3720f1c028af502.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afefe3720f1c028af502.png?alt=media\"/></p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let p : The switch S<sub>1</sub></p>\n<p>      q : The switch S<sub>2</sub></p>\n<p>The logical expression for the given circuit is p ∧ (~ p ∨ ~ q) ∧ q</p>\n<p>    p ∧ (~ p ∨ ~ q) ∧ q</p>\n<p>≡ [p ∧ (~ p ∨ ~ q] ∧ q   ...[Associative Law]</p>\n<p>≡ [(p ∧ ~ p) ∨ (p ∧ ~ q)] ∧ q   ...[Distributive Law]</p>\n<p>≡ [F ∨ (p ∧ ~ q)] ∧ q   ...[Complement Law]</p>\n<p>≡ (p ∧ ~ q) ∧ q   ...[Identity Law]</p>\n<p>≡ p ∧ (~ q ∧ q)   ...[Associative Law]</p>\n<p>≡ p ∧ F   ...[Complement Law]</p>\n<p>≡ F   ...[Identity Law]</p>\n<p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> The lamp will not glow irrespective of the status of the switches.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d14860780f","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d14860780f","q":"<p>Without using truth table prove that (p ∧ q) ∨ (∼ p ∧ q) v (p∧ ∼ q) ≡ p ∨ q</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>L.H.S. = (p ∧ q) ∨ (∼ p ∧ q) v (p∧ ∼ q) </p>\n<p>= [(p∨ ∼ p) ∧ q] ∨ (p∧ ∼ q)  ......(Distributive law)</p>\n<p>≡ (T ∧ q) ∨ (p∧ ∼ q)  .......(Complement law)</p>\n<p>≡ q ∨ (p∧ ∼ q)  ......(Identity law)</p>\n<p>≡ (q ∨ p) ∧ T   .......(Complement law)</p>\n<p>= q ∨ p  ......(Identity law)</p>\n<p>= p ∨ q   ......(Commutative law)</p>\n<p>= R.H.S</p>\n<p>Hence proved.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077de","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077de","q":"<p><strong>Find the symbolic form of the given switching circuit. Construct its switching table and interpret your result.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fhsc_maharashtra%252F12%252Fpublic%252F6941afd9e3720f1c028af4f7.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afd9e3720f1c028af4f7.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fhsc_maharashtra%2F12%2Fpublic%2F6941afd9e3720f1c028af4f7.png?alt=media\"/></strong></p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let p, q denote the statements that the switches S<sub>1</sub>, S<sub>2</sub> are closed respectively.</p>\n<p>Let ~p, ~q denote the statements that switches `\"S\"_1^\"'\"` and `\"S\"_2^\"'\"` are closed respectively.</p>\n<p>The symbolic form of the given switching circuit is (p ∨ q) ∧ (~p ∧ ~q) ≡ l</p>\n<p>The switching table for the given switching circuit is as follows: </p>\n<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>1</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>2</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>3</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>4</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>5</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>6</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>7</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>p</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>~p</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>~q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>p ∨ q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>~p ∧ ~q</strong></td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\"><strong>5 ∧ 6</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>In the last column of the switching table, each entry is zero, i.e. it is a contradiction.</p>\n<p>Hence, no current will flow in the circuit irrespective of the positions of the switches.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Mathematical Logic","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"}]}